# Single branch: main only

- Every change anywhere in the repository — website, mod, tools, contracts, assets, docs — is
  committed directly to **`main`**, with a focused commit message
  ([`CLAUDE.md`](/CLAUDE.md) law 2).
- Never create, check out or push a branch by hand: no `git checkout -b`, no `git switch -c`, and
  no workflow that needs a pull request.
- The one exception is the `slice/<id>` branches that the xtask tooling creates, merges and
  deletes itself: `cargo xtask platform slice-worktree` creates and drops them, and
  `cargo xtask mod wave` (the mod program) or `cargo xtask platform wave` (the platform) lands them
  ([Mod slice workflow](/documentation_v2/runbooks/mod_slice_workflow.md)).
- A stray branch found on the remote or in the checkout is merged into `main` and deleted.
